**No.** V3 is much closer, but I do not yet agree it is ready to execute as a production plan. It still needs to show that both meanings in a merged record reach the judge, that the real entry points use the split, and that acceptance can detect missed facts and wrong judgments.

A concrete example: one saved sentence reports both **$81.6 billion of total revenue** and **$75.2 billion of data-center revenue**. V3 says to preserve both summaries, but its stated test stops at the stored record; the current judge reads one `one_line` per record.

## 1. The seven round-3 disagreements

| # | Resolved? | Reason and evidence |
|---|---|---|
| **1. Identical quotations can lose a distinct statement** | **Partly — blocker** | V3 now requires both summaries and their respective links to survive, which addresses the observed loss. But the accepting test only says the record carries both; it does not explicitly prove that each question’s daily judge receives the right summary and attribution. The current judge reads one `one_line` and one set of source fields per record. The saved control has two meanings and destinations, while its current handover retains only the total-revenue summary. Prove the result through the real writer **and each judge input**, including a case with conflicting source fields. [Saved control](</Users/lchingen/hivemind-no-preseed-evidence-review/poc/data/parallel-b-link-2026-11-05-v2/gnews_3df0bbc8aff2c1d008bc0a32-control-3/result.json>), [v3 C-1](</Users/lchingen/hivemind-no-preseed-evidence-review/docs/research/2026-11-05-production-plan/plan-v3.md:10>), [judge input](</Users/lchingen/hivemind-no-preseed-evidence-review/src/hivemind/views/judging.py:121>). |
| **2. Split-aware preflight and production entry points** | **Partly — blocker** | C-6 restores request reconstruction, replay of checks, and reporting of skipped or empty checks. C-7 restores versioned prompts, configuration, replay selection, and freeze checks. It does **not** explicitly require the service entry point or test the split as a user invokes each real entry point. V0 named both replay and service; v3 names only replay. Byte-identical moved-code handovers alone do not establish that the production entry points select that code. [v3 C-6 and C-7](</Users/lchingen/hivemind-no-preseed-evidence-review/docs/research/2026-11-05-production-plan/plan-v3.md:48>), [v0 production path](</Users/lchingen/hivemind-no-preseed-evidence-review/docs/research/2026-11-05-production-plan/plan-v0.md:18>). |
| **3. An open-ended floor cannot be a finite middle result** | **Yes, as a plan** | V3 withdraws the rule and tests two ladder constructions against the frozen judge, including the judge’s own account. It does not claim the judge is innocent. The actual diagnosis and any change remain to be proved; a required change to frozen judging goes to Alex. [v3 §0.3](</Users/lchingen/hivemind-no-preseed-evidence-review/docs/research/2026-11-05-production-plan/plan-v3.md:12>), [seq 1273](</Users/lchingen/hivemind-no-preseed-evidence-review/docs/research/2026-11-05-production-plan/traces/split-v2-confirm-first100-2026-11-05/1273.json>). |
| **4. Refusing a supported run-on passage conflicts with D266** | **Yes, as to the disagreement** | V3 withdraws the blanket refusal and keeps the copied passage under D266. It also sends the remaining source/summary mismatch to Alex. In seq 1243, the stored quote ends after the reported purchase price, but the summary and attribution also describe the later anonymous-source passage. The later passage exists in the article; the problem is that the stored quotation alone does not support all the detail presented beside it. [Seq 1243](</Users/lchingen/hivemind-no-preseed-evidence-review/docs/research/2026-11-05-production-plan/traces/split-v2-confirm-first100-2026-11-05/1243.json:16>), [D266](</Users/lchingen/hivemind-no-preseed-evidence-review/docs/DECISIONS-log.md:3092>), [v3](</Users/lchingen/hivemind-no-preseed-evidence-review/docs/research/2026-11-05-production-plan/plan-v3.md:13>). |
| **5. Missing evidence, meaning, period, identity and daily judgments** | **Partly — serious** | V3 adds source-to-record and judge-input review by field, omission diagnosis, and a subject-identity restart test. That is a substantial improvement. It still needs an explicit test of the **actual judgment and its reason** for the double-growth cases, as well as the floors; an independent review of fields received does not by itself prove the judge used them correctly. The saved seq 1240 is the example that exposed the double-growth concern. [v3 C-4, C-7 and C-8](</Users/lchingen/hivemind-no-preseed-evidence-review/docs/research/2026-11-05-production-plan/plan-v3.md:34>), [seq 1240](</Users/lchingen/hivemind-no-preseed-evidence-review/docs/research/2026-11-05-production-plan/traces/split-v2-confirm-first100-2026-11-05/1240.json>). |
| **6. Independent, predeclared acceptance** | **Partly — serious** | V3 adds complete-source reading before outputs, three draws, same-day controls, prewritten stopping conditions, per-item losses, filing and judgment counts. It still leaves the exact independent reference, judgment criteria, and pass/fail thresholds to be defined. More fundamentally, it presents the historical seeded measurement and the unseeded production-shaped measurement as alternatives; the former cannot establish unseeded behavior, while the latter does not replace the required frozen-ruler acceptance. The arrangement goes to Alex, but the plan must state what each can and cannot establish. [v3 C-8](</Users/lchingen/hivemind-no-preseed-evidence-review/docs/research/2026-11-05-production-plan/plan-v3.md:58>), [AGENTS §5 and §7.1](</Users/lchingen/hivemind-no-preseed-evidence-review/AGENTS.md>), [D370](</Users/lchingen/hivemind-no-preseed-evidence-review/docs/DECISIONS-log.md:3998>). |
| **7. Claims of cause exceeded the probes** | **Yes** | V3 now calls the model accounts and missing unit instruction leads, not established causes. It says the two-send, five-item wording probe shows variation and cannot rule out an effect. That matches the limited evidence. [v3 §0.7](</Users/lchingen/hivemind-no-preseed-evidence-review/docs/research/2026-11-05-production-plan/plan-v3.md:16>), [probe results](</Users/lchingen/hivemind-no-preseed-evidence-review/poc/data/a-plural-probe-2026-11-05/results.json>). |

## 2. New serious problems in v3

**Serious — resolving conflicting attribution by always choosing B is unproven.** V3 says that when merged versions disagree on speaker, original speaker, original day or tier, it keeps B’s fields because B carries the tier rules. A rule shown to B does not establish that B’s answer is correct. In seq 1243, B’s retained quotation is shortened while its source description and summary still refer to the later passage. That is evidence that B’s fields need checking against the relevant source, not automatic precedence. This example does **not** demonstrate an actual A-versus-B conflict; it shows why B cannot be assumed authoritative when one occurs. The standard requires the original speaker, uncertainty and dates to be preserved faithfully. Count and inspect actual conflicts before choosing a general resolution. [v3 §0.1](</Users/lchingen/hivemind-no-preseed-evidence-review/docs/research/2026-11-05-production-plan/plan-v3.md:10>), [seq 1243](</Users/lchingen/hivemind-no-preseed-evidence-review/docs/research/2026-11-05-production-plan/traces/split-v2-confirm-first100-2026-11-05/1243.json:33>), [standard §5.4](</Users/lchingen/hivemind-no-preseed-evidence-review/docs/prd/05-extraction-standard.html:408>).

**Serious — the proposed historical fixture has no executable production-path arrangement yet.** V3 proposes the 22 seeds as a labelled measurement fixture, but the current replay entry point explicitly refuses a ledger containing seeded questions. The label explains the intent; it does not say how the measurement will pass through the real split path without changing the unseeded product behavior or bypassing the relevant checks. This is a plan gap, not evidence that such a fixture is impossible. [v3 C-8](</Users/lchingen/hivemind-no-preseed-evidence-review/docs/research/2026-11-05-production-plan/plan-v3.md:58>), [replay refusal](</Users/lchingen/hivemind-no-preseed-evidence-review/scripts/replay.py:29>), [D370](</Users/lchingen/hivemind-no-preseed-evidence-review/docs/DECISIONS-log.md:3998>).

## 3. Remaining disagreements

- **Blocker:** Prove merged meanings and their correct source information reach each affected daily judge through the real writer.
- **Blocker:** Specify and test every real production entry point, including the service, with the versioned split.
- **Serious:** Check actual daily judgment reasons for the double-growth cases, not only the fields delivered.
- **Serious:** Define what each acceptance measurement proves, its independent reference and decision criteria, and how the frozen seeded fixture runs through the real path.
- **Serious:** Do not automatically prefer B’s conflicting attribution fields without evidence that this resolves the counted conflicts correctly.

This was a read-only review. I inspected the cited records and code; I did not edit files, run the pipeline, or make model calls.